<title>USA: U.S. Gulf rigs under contract up 2 at 162.</title>
<headline>U.S. Gulf rigs under contract up 2 at 162.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>There were 162 rigs under contract in the U.S. Gulf as of January 17, up two from the period ending January 10, Offshore Data Services said Friday.</p>
<p>The utilization rate for rigs working in the Gulf, based on a total fleet of 183, was 88.5 percent.</p>
<p>The number of working rigs in the European/Mediterranean area dropped one this week to 105 rigs under contract out of a total fleet of 106, a utilization rate of 99.1 pct.</p>
<p>The worldwide rig count remained the same at 557 out of a total fleet of 606, making the utilization rate 91.9 percent.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk 212-859-1620</p>
</text>
